<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34783" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Perdiccas</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Perdicca</span></b> , ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Περδίκκας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Perdiccas</i>, <i>a Macedonian general
				under Alexander the Great</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 3, 9,
				7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 3,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 6, 19</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Tusc. 5, 12, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 13,
				2, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 6,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Eum. 3,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The name of three kings of Macedonia</i>, esp. <i>Perdiccas III.</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 7, 4,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 5,
			6</span></i>.</div>
